WEBVTT

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:11.220
The history of gaming extends 5,000 
years into the past to ancient Egypt.

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:15.720
Ancient games foretold the 
futures of men and kings.

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:19.200
They were magic ceremonies that 
determined a person's fate.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.340
These ceremonies were known 
as the "Shadow Games."

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.990
In the present, a young boy 
solves the Millennium Puzzle.

00:00:26.990 --> 00:00:30.210
He becomes the heir to the Shadow Games.

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:38.300
This boy possesses two hearts - 
one of light and one of darkness.

00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:42.210
He is known as "Yu-Gi-Oh."

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:50.340
I can't finish reading the magazine pages

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:57.250
I get the feeling that I must read it

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:04.000
Game cartridges are stacked 
in the corner of the room

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:10.700
Is there no meaning if I don't play them?

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:15.800
You're on the other side of the table

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:19.170
I'm talking to you, but...

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:26.100
You don't change your 
facial expression at all

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:32.350
Even though I'm this close to you

00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:39.620
These feelings don't reach 
you, don't reach you

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:46.360
What is truly precious?

00:01:50.070 --> 00:01:55.880
Gorgeous Harpie Lady

00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:05.320
Two hours have passed since the duels began.

00:02:06.710 --> 00:02:12.520
Yugi boy, will you be able to 
battle your way to my castle?

00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:21.440
All right, it's my turn!

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:23.890
I'll find someone to duel!

00:02:24.790 --> 00:02:27.630
Will Jonouchi be okay?

00:02:27.630 --> 00:02:31.800
All the duelists on this island are powerful.

00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:36.530
Come check this out!  The view's great!

00:02:36.530 --> 00:02:38.510
He never gets nervous.

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:40.810
Does he think he's on a field trip?

00:02:41.630 --> 00:02:43.640
The view really is great.

00:02:43.950 --> 00:02:46.470
Big brother, I want to see the ocean!

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:48.920
Okay!  I'll take you there!

00:02:56.150 --> 00:03:00.230
Jonouchi, won't Mom get mad at us?

00:03:00.230 --> 00:03:03.410
Don't worry.  Leave that to me.

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:04.640
Okay!

00:03:07.390 --> 00:03:09.510
Jonouchi!

00:03:09.510 --> 00:03:10.440
Yeah!

00:03:21.350 --> 00:03:23.630
It's so pretty.

00:03:23.630 --> 00:03:25.150
It's freezing!

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:37.560
Aren't you glad we came?

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:39.210
Let's come again sometime.

00:03:39.710 --> 00:03:41.000
But....

00:03:41.350 --> 00:03:46.280
Even if Mom and Dad get divorced and 
we have to live apart, don't worry.

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:48.190
I'll still take you here.

00:03:48.190 --> 00:03:49.860
You promise?

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:52.000
Yeah, I promise.

00:03:58.830 --> 00:04:02.350
Shizuka, I'll keep my promise.

00:04:02.350 --> 00:04:05.230
I'll let you see that beautiful ocean again.

00:04:05.230 --> 00:04:06.430
I promise.

00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:10.720
Look!

00:04:11.190 --> 00:04:13.360
Wow!

00:04:14.830 --> 00:04:17.480
Over there!  And here too!

00:04:19.540 --> 00:04:22.310
Everyone has started dueling.

00:04:22.310 --> 00:04:23.870
And so will I!

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:27.150
You should start off by finding 
the weakest duelist you can.

00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:28.320
That's right.

00:04:29.470 --> 00:04:33.970
Jonouchi, you should also choose 
where you duel carefully.

00:04:33.970 --> 00:04:36.710
Because depending on the field, my monsters

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:39.290
will have advantages and 
disadvantages, right Yugi?

00:04:39.290 --> 00:04:44.300
Right.  Everyone on this island should 
have figured out the rules by now.

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:46.380
Which field is best for you, Jonouchi?

00:04:46.380 --> 00:04:52.230
Since I have many Warrior and Beast-Warrior 
cards, the Sogen grassland would be best.

00:04:52.230 --> 00:04:56.550
That means this territory is ideal.

00:04:56.550 --> 00:04:59.710
Then you should probably stay here.

00:04:59.710 --> 00:05:02.870
Leave your Star Chips and get out of here!

00:05:02.870 --> 00:05:06.290
A voice that loud can only 
belong to Mai Kujaku!

00:05:06.460 --> 00:05:11.580
How could you tell which card you 
had while they were still facedown?

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:14.720
It's a secret.

00:05:16.990 --> 00:05:19.190
I'm one step closer to the money prize!

00:05:22.110 --> 00:05:25.240
She already has four Star Chips.

00:05:26.670 --> 00:05:29.990
Hi, Yugi!  Are your duels going well?

00:05:29.990 --> 00:05:31.270
Yeah, I guess so.

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:33.920
Yugi, you have three Star Chips?

00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:35.710
Maybe I'll duel you.

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:39.480
Yugi, make mince meat out of that girl.

00:05:40.070 --> 00:05:44.010
I decided that I want to duel right now.

00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:48.660
And I'm challenging Jonouchi.

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:50.950
What?  Me?

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:53.040
Don't run away, kid.

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:55.590
So I'm a marked man.

00:05:55.590 --> 00:05:57.140
Don't get the wrong idea.

00:05:57.550 --> 00:06:02.710
As a duelist, of course 
I want to battle Yugi.

00:06:02.710 --> 00:06:06.380
But if I run out of Star 
Chips, it's all over.

00:06:06.380 --> 00:06:12.440
I'll beat the weak duelists first so that I can 
get more Star Chips, then I'll battle Yugi later.

00:06:13.150 --> 00:06:15.560
I made the quaterfinals, you know!

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:17.880
But that was in the city tournament.

00:06:18.150 --> 00:06:20.430
There's no way you can defeat her.

00:06:20.430 --> 00:06:24.080
If you lose even once, you're done.

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:27.770
Yugi, take Jonouchi's place and duel her.

00:06:31.270 --> 00:06:32.760
Jonouchi.

00:06:33.070 --> 00:06:34.270
You have to do it.

00:06:34.270 --> 00:06:37.630
Yeah!  I knew you would say that, Yugi.

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:38.670
Yugi!

00:06:38.670 --> 00:06:39.750
You can't be serious, Jonouchi.

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:41.830
I am serious!  Super serious!

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:54.020
If I run away, every time I look at the sky, 
the mountains or the ocean in the future...

00:06:54.020 --> 00:07:00.800
Every time I see what we're currently 
seeing, it'll remind me of how I was a coward.

00:07:01.110 --> 00:07:05.540
I understand.  Sorry, Jonouchi.

00:07:05.710 --> 00:07:08.230
If you're going to duel, then you better win!

00:07:08.230 --> 00:07:10.040
I accept your duel.

00:07:10.230 --> 00:07:12.000
That's the spirit.

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:17.510
Jonouchi, fight hard!

00:07:17.510 --> 00:07:18.830
Don't lose!

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:19.890
Yeah!

00:07:21.110 --> 00:07:22.390
Jonouchi.

00:07:22.990 --> 00:07:25.470
You only have one Star Chip, right?

00:07:25.470 --> 00:07:28.680
So I'll only wager one.

00:07:28.950 --> 00:07:32.250
If I lose this Star Chip, it's all over.

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:34.390
Oh no!

00:07:34.790 --> 00:07:36.560
Not this field!

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:45.140
Our field is 40% Mountain, 
40% Sogen and 20% Wasteland.

00:07:45.140 --> 00:07:48.040
Stay calm, Jonouchi.  You'll be fine.

00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:51.380
Your cards will have an advantage 
on the Sogen part of the field.

00:07:51.560 --> 00:07:53.040
Yeah.

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:54.480
Mai Kujaku!

00:07:54.750 --> 00:07:57.720
I want to ask you one thing 
before we start our duel.

00:07:58.350 --> 00:07:59.430
What?

00:07:59.430 --> 00:08:02.270
Why did you come to this island?

00:08:02.270 --> 00:08:05.250
Glory?  Or money?

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:06.570
For both.

00:08:06.570 --> 00:08:10.310
If I win the prize money, 
I'd travel around the world,

00:08:10.310 --> 00:08:13.570
buy an apartment in France and 
a bunch of designer brands.

00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:16.440
That's a pathetic reason.

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:21.310
How rude!  So why are you here?

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:27.280
There's something that I want to protect, 
and I must protect it with my life.

00:08:27.830 --> 00:08:30.990
Jonouchi, show that you're fighting 
for much more than she is!

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:32.160
Duel!

00:08:33.860 --> 00:08:35.690
It's my turn.

00:08:35.690 --> 00:08:37.960
Masaki the Legendary Swordsman.

00:08:39.990 --> 00:08:44.240
The Sogen Field Power Source powers it up!

00:08:44.240 --> 00:08:47.000
It's your turn.

00:08:53.870 --> 00:08:55.250
Why won't you look at your cards?

00:08:55.430 --> 00:09:00.120
It's simple.  Because I already 
know what these cards are.

00:09:00.710 --> 00:09:01.490
Impossible!

00:09:01.710 --> 00:09:03.290
What?

00:09:03.290 --> 00:09:06.160
Here I go.  My card is...

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:09.840
Harpie Lady!

00:09:13.350 --> 00:09:16.360
It's suited for the Mountain 
field, so it powers up.

00:09:18.270 --> 00:09:20.800
I'll battle it!  Go!

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:27.750
No, Jonouchi!  Harpie Lady 
has the ability to fly!

00:09:31.550 --> 00:09:36.830
Flying monsters have magical 
resistance against land monsters.

00:09:36.830 --> 00:09:38.510
What do you mean?

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:42.840
Masaki's attack and defense 
points both return to 1100.

00:09:54.510 --> 00:09:56.280
Your turn, kid.

00:09:56.550 --> 00:09:58.080
She didn't look at her card again.

00:09:58.080 --> 00:09:59.510
Jonouchi...

00:09:59.510 --> 00:10:02.340
Isn't there any way Jonouchi can win?

00:10:02.340 --> 00:10:06.090
Jonouchi, don't let her 
card tricks deceive you.

00:10:06.090 --> 00:10:09.090
How can she know her cards 
when they're facedown?

00:10:10.590 --> 00:10:15.790
My card trick has taken him off his game.

00:10:15.790 --> 00:10:18.700
He lost even before the duel began.

00:10:20.030 --> 00:10:22.040
Tiger Axe!

00:10:22.950 --> 00:10:26.710
The Field Power raises its attack points.

00:10:26.990 --> 00:10:29.710
Defeat Harpie Lady with mutual destruction!

00:10:29.910 --> 00:10:32.950
Jonouchi, you forgot that 
it's resistant to magic!

00:10:33.190 --> 00:10:36.840
That's right!  Tiger Axe's 
attack points don't change!

00:10:44.190 --> 00:10:48.900
You'll need stronger cards than 
that to defeat my Harpie Lady.

00:10:48.900 --> 00:10:50.600
My turn.

00:10:51.710 --> 00:10:57.430
With each turn, my Harpie Lady 
gets more beautiful and powerful.

00:10:57.430 --> 00:10:59.710
She played another card 
without looking at it.

00:10:59.710 --> 00:11:01.200
What's going on?

00:11:02.670 --> 00:11:04.640
I'll try to survive by defending.

00:11:05.350 --> 00:11:07.040
It's my turn.

00:11:07.630 --> 00:11:11.550
I'll dress up my Harpie 
Lady with Cyber Shield.

00:11:24.590 --> 00:11:26.600
My Kojikocy...

00:11:27.350 --> 00:11:32.040
Now do you realize that you're 
nothing more than my victim?

00:11:32.230 --> 00:11:34.680
Why does she know her facedown cards?

00:11:34.680 --> 00:11:37.840
Does she have psychic powers?

00:11:55.330 --> 00:12:00.710
Calm down, Jonouchi.  Don't get 
fooled by Mai's card tricks.

00:12:00.710 --> 00:12:02.360
You can do it, Jonouchi!

00:12:02.360 --> 00:12:05.480
Don't let that arrogant girl beat you!

00:12:05.480 --> 00:12:07.280
Hey you!

00:12:07.740 --> 00:12:12.750
You said earlier that your hearts 
will reach the person who's dueling.

00:12:12.990 --> 00:12:19.690
Then let's see you use your hearts 
to make that weak kid win.

00:12:19.690 --> 00:12:21.220
What?

00:12:21.220 --> 00:12:23.040
Do you now understand?

00:12:23.040 --> 00:12:25.380
That's impossible.

00:12:25.380 --> 00:12:27.110
Remember that, kid.

00:12:27.110 --> 00:12:31.510
If you care about friendship, you'll 
never become a true duelist.

00:12:31.510 --> 00:12:34.920
Your friend today might 
be your enemy tomorrow.

00:12:34.920 --> 00:12:37.210
That's what dueling is all about.

00:12:37.510 --> 00:12:40.670
A duelist must only trust herself.

00:12:40.670 --> 00:12:44.680
Let today's defeat be a lesson to you.

00:12:45.840 --> 00:12:47.030
How dare she!

00:12:47.030 --> 00:12:50.280
This is frustrating!

00:12:58.870 --> 00:13:03.930
We will make Jonouchi win 
with just one phrase.

00:13:04.670 --> 00:13:05.500
Yugi?

00:13:05.750 --> 00:13:10.100
Jonouchi, think about the 
phrase that I'm about to say.

00:13:10.270 --> 00:13:12.870
What can be seen but remains unseen?

00:13:12.870 --> 00:13:15.760
Seen but remains unseen?

00:13:17.870 --> 00:13:21.190
He's going to win because of that phrase?

00:13:21.190 --> 00:13:24.510
How interesting.  Let's see that happen.

00:13:24.510 --> 00:13:27.150
I know what you mean, but...

00:13:28.830 --> 00:13:35.560
It's friendship.  We can see each 
other, but we can't see friendship.

00:13:36.390 --> 00:13:40.930
But that's not enough 
for me to win this time.

00:13:41.230 --> 00:13:45.320
It's unfortunate for me that I can't see you.

00:13:45.320 --> 00:13:49.070
I wanted to see your face one last time.

00:13:49.260 --> 00:13:53.730
Shizuka, you deserve a better brother.

00:13:53.730 --> 00:13:57.840
I'm not even able to save her eyesight.

00:13:57.840 --> 00:13:58.750
Damn!

00:14:06.750 --> 00:14:11.250
If you can no longer see, is 
the whole world dark like this?

00:14:11.830 --> 00:14:14.520
I don't want to send you into this world.

00:14:17.990 --> 00:14:19.670
What's that smell?

00:14:21.910 --> 00:14:25.310
I never noticed it when I had my eyes open.

00:14:25.440 --> 00:14:27.920
I smell various perfumes.

00:14:30.030 --> 00:14:32.430
Kid, it's your turn.

00:14:32.430 --> 00:14:35.790
That's it!  I figured out your card trick!

00:14:36.950 --> 00:14:40.800
You sprayed each of your cards 
with different perfumes.

00:14:42.030 --> 00:14:44.220
By smelling the different scents,

00:14:44.220 --> 00:14:46.930
you could tell which card was 
which, even if they were facedown.

00:14:47.510 --> 00:14:51.010
You can see cards, but you can't see odors.

00:14:51.010 --> 00:14:52.940
That's what's seen but remains unseen!

00:14:53.150 --> 00:14:54.280
No way!

00:14:54.280 --> 00:14:58.540
How could this amateur 
solve my aroma tactics?

00:14:58.540 --> 00:15:03.720
Your trick took me off my game 
even before the duel began.

00:15:03.720 --> 00:15:07.080
I was scared because I was 100% 
sure that it was the occult.

00:15:07.080 --> 00:15:10.830
But I won't be fooled anymore, you cheater!

00:15:10.830 --> 00:15:11.820
Jonouchi!

00:15:11.820 --> 00:15:12.930
Jonouchi!

00:15:12.930 --> 00:15:14.070
Go for it!

00:15:14.070 --> 00:15:15.660
Yugi, thank you!

00:15:15.660 --> 00:15:22.210
Even if you figured out my trick, you 
still won't defeat me in a million years!

00:15:22.210 --> 00:15:26.380
Isn't it strange that since I 
know my friends have my back,

00:15:26.380 --> 00:15:29.410
I feel that I can defeat you easily?

00:15:29.910 --> 00:15:33.920
But that's a concept you won't 
understand in a million years.

00:15:34.470 --> 00:15:37.980
Here I go.  My card is Baby Dragon.

00:15:37.980 --> 00:15:39.520
That card!

00:15:45.710 --> 00:15:47.930
Look at that wimpy card!

00:15:48.120 --> 00:15:53.170
Even if I destroy that card, 
you won't lose any life points.

00:15:53.390 --> 00:15:56.190
I play Elegant Egotist.

00:15:56.190 --> 00:15:59.800
This card creates copies of my Harpie Lady!

00:16:02.900 --> 00:16:04.620
What?

00:16:04.620 --> 00:16:08.350
Harpie Lady 1... 2... 3!

00:16:09.310 --> 00:16:11.080
She now has more!

00:16:11.080 --> 00:16:14.310
Oh no!  He was having trouble with just one!

00:16:14.310 --> 00:16:15.920
Don't give up, Jonouchi!

00:16:15.920 --> 00:16:17.440
There must be something you can do!

00:16:17.440 --> 00:16:19.190
Like what?

00:16:19.190 --> 00:16:22.090
Don't ask an amateur like me!  Well, Yugi?

00:16:22.090 --> 00:16:25.040
It's too early to say 
whether he'll lose or not.

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:29.400
I don't have any cards that can 
defeat three Harpie Ladies.

00:16:29.990 --> 00:16:32.870
This is the Harpie Ladies' 
gorgeous ten-cycle combo!

00:16:32.870 --> 00:16:36.840
As each turn passes, they transform 
and become more powerful.

00:16:37.010 --> 00:16:41.350
Since I played Elegant Egotist, I can't 
attack this turn.  It's your turn.

00:16:41.510 --> 00:16:44.510
But I'm sure there's nothing you can do.

00:16:44.510 --> 00:16:46.000
I really can't win.

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:47.720
This is the end.

00:16:47.720 --> 00:16:50.220
Don't give up, Jonouchi.

00:16:50.760 --> 00:16:54.700
Mai Kujaku's ten-cycle combo 
uses dozens of spell cards

00:16:54.700 --> 00:16:57.760
to power up a single Harpie Lady.

00:16:58.040 --> 00:17:01.370
But her strategy has a fatal flaw.

00:17:01.370 --> 00:17:04.390
A fatal flaw?  I see!

00:17:04.390 --> 00:17:07.140
If she needs to use dozens of spell cards,

00:17:07.140 --> 00:17:10.610
Harpie Lady must be the only 
monster card in her deck.

00:17:10.870 --> 00:17:14.610
If I defeat her Harpie Ladies, 
there's nothing else she can do.

00:17:14.790 --> 00:17:16.560
That's right, Jonouchi.

00:17:16.560 --> 00:17:19.950
Once again, it's what can 
be seen but remains unseen.

00:17:19.950 --> 00:17:22.320
What can be seen but remains unseen...

00:17:23.660 --> 00:17:25.220
Come to think of it...

00:17:25.220 --> 00:17:31.710
Salamandra, Kunai with Chain, 
Baby Dragon and Shield & Sword.

00:17:31.710 --> 00:17:36.470
With these spell cards, you'll 
have more strategies than before.

00:17:36.470 --> 00:17:37.400
I see.

00:17:37.400 --> 00:17:40.270
Oh yeah.  Use this.

00:17:40.480 --> 00:17:43.350
It should help in an emergency.

00:17:43.350 --> 00:17:45.240
I remember now.

00:17:46.030 --> 00:17:48.280
That was the Millennium Puzzle's box.

00:17:48.280 --> 00:17:53.550
The Millennium Puzzle's riddle was also 
"that which can be seen but remains unseen."

00:17:53.550 --> 00:17:55.870
That means it's Time Wizard!

00:17:55.870 --> 00:17:57.700
Stop wasting time!

00:17:57.700 --> 00:18:00.160
Play your card already!

00:18:00.160 --> 00:18:03.520
Time Wizard isn't in my hand.

00:18:03.520 --> 00:18:07.960
I have to draw it before 
she destroys Baby Dragon.

00:18:08.790 --> 00:18:09.400
Please!

00:18:09.630 --> 00:18:12.320
Jonouchi, believe in your cards!

00:18:14.470 --> 00:18:16.800
Here I go.  Now!

00:18:20.590 --> 00:18:24.320
All right!  Time Wizard!

00:18:27.030 --> 00:18:28.420
Time Wizard?

00:18:28.420 --> 00:18:30.230
Don't you know?

00:18:30.230 --> 00:18:36.230
A thousand years will pass, allowing Baby 
Dragon to grow into Thousand Dragon.

00:18:36.230 --> 00:18:40.640
Jonouchi, that's not Time 
Wizard's only effect.

00:18:40.640 --> 00:18:42.300
Time Magic!

00:18:51.070 --> 00:18:53.950
Transform into Thousand Dragon!

00:18:54.430 --> 00:18:56.750
That Dragon is pathetic.

00:18:56.750 --> 00:18:59.720
My Harpie Ladies have higher attack points!

00:18:59.720 --> 00:19:02.880
Destroy it, Harpie Lady Sisters!

00:19:03.960 --> 00:19:09.480
What?  My Harpies are old and weak!

00:19:09.910 --> 00:19:13.090
He told you that a million 
years had passed, so

00:19:13.090 --> 00:19:16.200
your Harpies became old 
and lost their strength.

00:19:16.430 --> 00:19:18.890
Mai Kujaku, it must be 
especially cruel for you

00:19:18.890 --> 00:19:22.570
because you're losing beauty 
along with this duel.

00:19:23.630 --> 00:19:25.400
That surprised me too!

00:19:25.400 --> 00:19:26.210
All right!

00:19:26.430 --> 00:19:29.440
Go, Thousand Dragon!

00:19:32.250 --> 00:19:34.960
Thousand Nose Breath!

00:19:44.950 --> 00:19:46.830
He did it!  It's a miracle!

00:19:46.830 --> 00:19:48.600
Jonouchi won!

00:19:48.600 --> 00:19:49.880
Yugi!

00:19:51.950 --> 00:19:56.150
How could I lose to someone like him?

00:19:56.150 --> 00:19:57.440
Mai Kujaku!

00:19:58.110 --> 00:20:02.340
I may not be a true duelist, 
but I can say this:

00:20:02.340 --> 00:20:06.000
Some things don't change, 
even after a thousand years.

00:20:06.550 --> 00:20:11.200
It's what can be seen but remains unseen.

00:20:14.430 --> 00:20:17.150
Jonouchi, the difference in what

00:20:17.150 --> 00:20:21.110
you were fighting for compared to 
hers was what led you to victory.

00:20:31.950 --> 00:20:34.050
I'm hungry!

00:20:34.050 --> 00:20:36.820
If you're running a tournament, you 
could at least have meals ready!

00:20:36.820 --> 00:20:38.590
Pegasus, you cheapskate!

00:20:38.590 --> 00:20:45.120
The ocean duelist Ryota Kajiki lures us 
with the delicious smell of grilled fish.

00:20:45.120 --> 00:20:48.900
With his Sea Stealth Attack, his monsters 
attack while hiding deep in the waters.

00:20:48.900 --> 00:20:50.870
Yugi is in big trouble!

00:20:50.870 --> 00:20:53.590
How can he fight against 
enemies that he can't see?

00:20:53.590 --> 00:20:56.390
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Kairyu-Shin

00:20:56.390 --> 00:20:58.400
Duel, standby!

00:21:02.060 --> 00:21:10.460
The flask glistens

00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:18.310
Wait for me in the science classroom

00:21:18.800 --> 00:21:27.280
If we put our cold hands together

00:21:27.980 --> 00:21:35.060
And rub them together, they become warm

00:21:36.760 --> 00:21:40.890
Shower of happiness

00:21:41.180 --> 00:21:45.000
I will shower you with it

00:21:45.330 --> 00:21:53.280
I will support you even when you feel lonely

00:21:53.480 --> 00:21:57.510
Shower of happiness

00:21:57.780 --> 00:22:01.640
You are not alone

00:22:02.020 --> 00:22:08.360
You're protected by a 
giant ring of friendship
